To create a similar image using JavaScript, you can use the HTML canvas element to draw the vehicles. Here's an example of how to draw a single car:
```javascript
// canvas element
const canvas = document.getElementById('canvas');

// drawing context
const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

// car image
const carImage = new Image();
carImage.src = 'car.png';

// draw car
function drawCar(x, y) {
  ctx.drawImage(carImage, x, y);
}

// draw all cars
for (let i = 0; i < cars.length; i++) {
  drawCar(cars[i].x, cars[i].y);
}
```
You can repeat this process for each vehicle type, creating a grid of vehicles. You can also use libraries like fabric.js to simplify the drawing process.

Note that this example uses a single car image, but in the original image, there are multiple types of vehicles. You would need to create separate images for each vehicle type and use the appropriate drawing functions to draw them.
